    "at_a_glance": {
      "type": "multicolumn-with-icons",
      "blocks": {
        "g_time": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "time",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "About 35 minutes",
            "text": "<p>15 minutes of prep and 20 of cooking. The broccoli roasts while the salmon sears, so the two finish together. Add 1&ndash;3 hours up front for the dry brine if you have them.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 2",
            "text": "<p>Two skin-on King Salmon portions. The recipe is written for 6 oz; ours come as 8.5 oz, so go by the thermometer rather than the clock and pull at 130&deg;F.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_brine": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Salt it early",
            "text": "<p>About &frac12; tsp Diamond Crystal per 6 oz portion, uncovered on a rack in the fridge for one to three hours. It seasons the flesh and dries the skin. Not overnight &mdash; fish firms up fast.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_rest": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Rest off the heat",
            "text": "<p>Partway through, the fillets come out and sit skin up on a rack for 4 minutes, with the pan <em>off</em> the burner. The middle catches up; the skin does not overcook.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
